  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Let \\(D=a^2+b^2+c^2,\\) where \\(a,\\) \\(b\\) are consecutive integers and \\(c=ab.\\) Then \\(\\sqrt D\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "always an even integer"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "sometimes an odd integer, sometimes not"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "always an odd integer"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "sometimes rational, sometimes not"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "always irrational"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1967-p31.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "With \\(b=a+1\\) and \\(c=a(a+1),\\) \\[ \\begin{aligned} D&=a^2+(a+1)^2+a^2(a+1)^2\\\\ &=(a^2+a+1)^2. \\end{aligned} \\] Thus \\(\\sqrt D=a^2+a+1.\\) Since \\(a(a+1)\\) is even, this integer is always odd.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Set \\(b=a+1\\) and expand \\(D\\)",
        "Try to recognize \\(D\\) as the square of \\(a^2+a+1\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
